"""Two-segment slow motion demo experiment.

This is a presentation-only workflow: it moves the stacked dual-segment
robot through a slow, smooth, visible command-space pattern (figure-8,
circle, sweep, clover, ...) and records what was commanded plus the live
servo telemetry. It is NOT data collection, NOT closed-loop control, NOT
model validation, and NOT physical-tip chasing. The metadata flags
``demo_only=True``, ``valid_for_model_training=False``, and
``valid_for_thesis_repeatability=False`` are stamped into every artifact.

Behavior summary:

* Trajectory is generated by ``continuum_robot.demo.two_segment_motion_patterns``.
* Each trajectory point's bottom/top tendon vector is rebuilt into a
  ``TwoSegmentCommand`` via the runtime ``RobotOperatingContext`` so the
  segment-a/segment-b assignment honors the physical bottom/top mapping.
* The flat 8-vector goes through ``_apply_top_routing_compensation`` and
  ``mapper.to_goal_positions`` exactly like the trusted collect-pose path.
* The bus write happens through ``ServoService._write_goal_positions``.
* Telemetry is read after each command for the trace; sustained overcurrent
  causes a fail-closed halt + best-effort return to neutral.
* Dry-run produces the trajectory and trace WITHOUT writing the bus.

This module deliberately depends on the existing safe command path. It
does not introduce any new motion path.
"""

